<big>'''The Open Witness Archive'''</big><br />
''An original-fiction archive of memory, revision, and the lives a correction can change.''
</div>

An evacuation bell rang in Leth. People remembered the sound and the lives it saved, but no one had rung it. [[Sovereign|Ivo Ren]], a municipal corrections clerk, found the missing cause and put it back. The bell rang again. A child was safe, and the child's mother no longer remembered the person who had rescued him.

That was Ivo's first lesson in [[Sovereign/Self-Refinement|revision]]: a better outcome can take something real away. Years later, people called him Sovereign because even a final account of what he was could sometimes be revised. He still carries a brass frame from the corrections office, still worries about a cup in his mother's kitchen, and still cannot prove that the one remembering his childhood is the one who lived it.

This archive keeps the stories, records, contradictions, and refusals that a list of powers would miss.

